Vertical Slice: The first room
Goal of the Slice
Prove that:
    • Crawling + throwing is fun
    • Vertical risk (towers) creates meaningful choices
    • Stealth vs chaos affects outcomes
    • Healing events reinforce player behavior
If this works, the rest of the game will work.

1. Level Layout (One Screen + Vertical Space)
Room Structure
    • Floor path (safe):
        ◦ Low cover
        ◦ Grass patches (extra stealth)
    • One tower (optional):
        ◦ 2–3 player-heights tall
        ◦ One ladder / climbable surface
    • Exit door on far side
    • Healing room immediately after

2. Enemies (Only 2 Types)
Enemy A: Floor Patrol
    • Patrols left ↔ right
    • Medium vision cone
    • Weak to stealth throws
    • Awareness states:
        ◦ Unaware → Suspicious → Alerted
Enemy B: Tower Sentry
    • Stationary on top of tower
    • Long vision cone
    • Poor awareness directly below
    • Can knock player off tower if Alerted
    • Falls and dies if pushed or stunned

3. Player Abilities (Locked for Slice)
Movement
    • Crawl (default)
    • Climb tower
Crawl Rules
    • Quiet
    • Can throw items
    • Harder to detect
Climb Rules
    • More visible
    • Cannot throw
    • Can be knocked off
    • Falling:
        ◦ Deals damage
        ◦ Alerts nearby enemies

4. Items (Keep It Minimal)
Throwable Items (3 Total)
    1. Small Junk
        ◦ Quiet
        ◦ Low damage
        ◦ Good for distractions
    2. Heavy Scrap
        ◦ Loud
        ◦ High damage
        ◦ Can knock enemies off towers
    3. Bottle
        ◦ Medium noise
        ◦ Shatters on impact
        ◦ Causes Suspicious state
Items are placed:
    • 2 on the floor
    • 1 near the tower base

5. Stealth Rules (Explicit)
    • Enemy hit while Unaware:
        ◦ Instant kill OR stun
        ◦ Bonus money drop
    • Killing tower enemy without alert:
        ◦ Extra crafting ingredient
    • Alerting enemies:
        ◦ Harder fight
        ◦ Slightly better money drop
This makes stealth a strategic choice.

6. Resource Drops (Small Numbers)
Floor Enemy Drops
    • 5 money
    • 1 ingredient (50% chance)
Tower Enemy Drops
    • 8 money
    • 1 ingredient (guaranteed if stealth killed)
This reinforces vertical risk.

7. Decision Paths (What the Player Learns)
Path 1: Safe Crawl
    • Avoid tower
    • Kill floor enemy quietly
    • Fewer rewards
    • Low risk
Path 2: Risky Climb
    • Climb tower
    • Take out sentry
    • Higher reward
    • Risk of fall and alert
Both are valid.

8. Healing Event (Immediately After)
Healing Event: “Catch Your Breath”
Choices:
    1. Train
        ◦ Choose:
            ▪ Human strength
            ▪ Alien strength
        ◦ No dialogue
    2. Talk to Alien
        ◦ Friendly
            ▪ +Relationship
        ◦ Hostile
            ▪ +Minor combat buff next room
            ▪ −Relationship
        ◦ Romantic (locked unless relationship ≥ threshold)
            ▪ If attempted too early → awkward → −Relationship
Dialogue text can be 1–2 lines only.

9. Success Criteria (Very Important)
The slice is successful if:
    • Players understand:
        ◦ Crawling = safety
        ◦ Towers = risk + reward
    • Players choose whether to climb
    • Players notice better rewards from stealth
    • Healing choices feel connected to playstyle
If players ignore towers or don’t notice rewards, redesign before adding content.

10. What NOT to Include
Do not add:
    • More enemies
    • More items
    • More dialogue
    • More rooms
This slice is about clarity, not quantity.

11. What to Build First (Order)
    1. Movement (crawl + climb)
    2. One enemy with awareness states
    3. Throwing items
    4. Tower interaction
    5. Healing event UI
